<title>USA: Bridgeport, Conn plans up to $50 mln bond sale.</title>
<headline>Bridgeport, Conn plans up to $50 mln bond sale.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bridgeport, Conn., plans to competitively sell during the next two weeks up to $50 million of general obligation bonds to pay for capital improvements, a spokesman for Mayor Joseph Ganim said Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;It'll be toward the end of next week or early the following week,&quot; said Chris Duby, the spokesman.</p>
